HU - Indentation-Structured Text Editor
===========================================

A modal terminal editor that uses indentation as the primary
structural signal. Works well with any indentation-based language
(Hoon, Python, YAML, Haskell, etc.).

Run:  node hu.js <file>


MODES
-----

  normal    Default mode. Navigate, fold, delete, yank, paste.
  insert    Type text. Enter with i/a/o, exit with Esc.
  select    Highlight lines or chars. Enter with Space/v.
  command   Ex-style commands. Enter with :
  search    Find text. Enter with /


NORMAL MODE
-----------

  Movement
    j / k           move down / up
    h / l           move left / right
    w / b           next / prev word
    J / K           next / prev sibling (same indent level)
    q / z           nearest less-indented line above / below
    g / G           top / bottom of file

  Folding
    Tab             toggle fold at cursor
    F               fold all foldable lines at cursor's indent
    E               expand all folds

  Editing
    d               delete line (yanks it)
    y               yank (copy) line
    p / P           paste below / above
    H / L           outdent / indent line
    o / O           open new line below / above (enters insert)
    u / r           undo / redo
    "               open yank register panel

  Mode switching
    i / a           insert before / after cursor
    I / A           insert at line start / end
    Space           start line selection
    v               start character selection
    /               search
    :               command mode
    :help           open this help file


INSERT MODE
-----------

    Esc             return to normal mode
    Home / End      beginning / end of line
    Arrows          move cursor
    Backspace       delete behind
    Delete          delete forward
    Tab             insert two spaces
    Shift-Tab       remove indent


SELECT MODE
-----------

    j / k           extend selection down / up
    Space           cycle unit: line > section > indent > parent
    d               delete selection
    y               yank selection
    H / L           outdent / indent selection
    Esc             cancel selection


COMMANDS  (type : then the command)
--------

    :w              save
    :q              quit
    :wq             save and quit
    :q!             force quit (discard changes)
    :123            go to line 123


ABOUT THIS TEST DIRECTORY
=========================

Each .hu file is a JSON test fixture that describes a sequence
of keystrokes and the expected editor state after each step.

Tests are organized into subdirectories by category:
  navigation/   cursor movement, word nav, sibling nav
  editing/      insert, delete, yank, paste, indent, undo
  folds/        fold/unfold, fold-all, fold navigation
  select/       line and char selection, unit cycling
  search/       find, next/prev match
  command/      ex-style commands

File format (frames style):

  {
    "desc": "description of what this test covers",
    "before": ["line one", "line two", "line three"],
    "frames": [
      {
        "desc": "press j to move down",
        "keys": ["j"],
        "after": ["line one", "line two", "line three"],
        "cursor": [1, 0]
      },
      {
        "desc": "delete the line",
        "keys": ["d"],
        "after": ["line one", "line three"],
        "cursor": [1, 0]
      }
    ]
  }

  "before"      starting buffer contents (array of lines)
  "beforeFolds" optional array of line numbers folded at start
  "frames"      sequence of steps, each with:
    "keys"      array of key names to press in order
    "desc"      what this step does
    "after"     expected buffer lines after the keys
    "cursor"    expected [line, col] position
    "mode"      expected mode (normal, insert, select)

Each test is a visual mockup: the before state, then each frame
as [keys] followed by the resulting after state.
